<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Give exact values or decimals to 2 decimal places.</p><p>(a) Find the magnitude of <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 15 \\ -8 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) On a map with 1 unit = 1 km, a school S is at <m>({1},\,{-4})</m> and a clinic K at <m>({-3},\,{0})</m>. How far is the clinic from the school in a straight line?</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> km  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Pythagoras on the across and up moves: <m>|\mathbf{v}| = \sqrt{x^2 + y^2}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>\sqrt{({15})^2 + ({-8})^2} = \sqrt{{289}}</m> <m>= {17}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>\overrightarrow{SK}</m> is end minus start: <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ 4 \end{array}\right)}</m>. Its magnitude is <m>\sqrt{({-4})^2 + ({4})^2} = \sqrt{{32}}</m> <m>\approx {5.66}</m> km.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>17</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2^{\frac{5}{2}}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>